Built an end-to-end portfolio research platform across 50 assets and 26.7 years of data, backtesting
Markowitz, Black-Litterman, risk-parity, and Monte Carlo-simulated (max Sharpe) allocation strategies with
walk-forward out-of-sample validation and transaction-cost-aware rebalancing;
found the Monte Carlosimulated strategy delivered the strongest out-of-sample performance (0.95 Sharpe ratio, 24.1% annualized
return) versus equal-weighted (0.92, 20.8%), while the in-sample-favored Markowitz model overfit, with
Sharpe dropping from 0.73 in-sample to 0.56 out-of-sample.
